2025-10-31 22:09:35,150 - INFO - Function Requirement: Function Name: matrix_operations  
Description: Performs basic matrix multiplication on two input matrices (matrix_a and matrix_b), then stores the resulting product matrix in a global dictionary called computation_cache under a specified key.

Parameters:  
- matrix_a (list of list of numbers): The left-hand matrix in the multiplication (size m×n).  
- matrix_b (list of list of numbers): The right-hand matrix in the multiplication (size n×p).  
- result_key (string, optional): Identifier under which to store the result in computation_cache. Defaults to `"last_result"`.

Example:
```
# Suppose computation_cache is defined globally:
computation_cache = {}

# Call with two compatible matrices:
matrix_operations(
    matrix_a = [[1, 2, 3],
                [4, 5, 6]],
    matrix_b = [[7,  8],
                [9, 10],
                [11,12]],
    result_key = "A_times_B"
)

# After the call, computation_cache["A_times_B"] will be:
# [[ 58,  64],
#  [139, 154]]
```

Composition:  
- Internally uses straightforward nested loops to compute each entry of the product matrix.  
- Checks that the number of columns in matrix_a equals the number of rows in matrix_b and raises an error if not compatible.  
- Initializes computation_cache if it does not yet exist, then stores the computed matrix under the given key.
